.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt PREVIEW 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm preview
.Nd preview Markdown files in the browser, rendered like GitHub
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl b
.Op Fl d Ar feature Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
.Op Fl H Ar host
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl -log-level Ar level
.Op Fl -mermaid-icon-pack Ar pack Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
.Op Fl -no-border
.Op Fl -no-reload
.Op Ar file | folder
.Nm
.Fl h | v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a small web server that renders Markdown files the way GitHub does.
It uses GitHub's stylesheets and colour themes, and supports tables,
task lists, alerts, footnotes, emoji, front matter, math and Mermaid
diagrams.
Everything it needs is built in, so it works without network access.
.Pp
Given a
.Ar file ,
.Nm
serves the folder that holds it and opens the file.
Given a
.Ar folder ,
it serves that folder and opens its folder page.
Without an argument it serves the current directory.
A path that does not exist is an error.
.Pp
A folder page lists the folder's entries, folders first, with size and
modification time, and renders the folder's README below the list, as
GitHub does.
Files ending in
.Pa .md ,
.Pa .markdown ,
.Pa .mdown ,
.Pa .mdwn ,
.Pa .mkd ,
.Pa .mkdn
or
.Pa .mkdown
are rendered.
Other files are served as they are, so images and links between
documents work.
.Pp
While a page is open,
.Nm
watches what it shows: the Markdown file and the local images it
references, or for a folder page, the folder's entries.
When one of them changes the page reloads.
Editor temporary and swap files are ignored.
.Pp
The buttons in the top right corner cycle the colour theme between
light, dark and dark dimmed, set the content width, switch to GitHub's
colorblind palette, and pause reloading for the open page.
Without a stored choice the theme follows the operating system.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b , -browser
Open the start page in the default browser.
.It Fl d , -disable Ar feature Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
Turn off Markdown features.
A
.Ar feature
is one of
.Cm details ,
.Cm footnote ,
.Cm ghissue ,
.Cm mathjax
or
.Cm mermaid .
The option can be repeated.
.It Fl H , -host Ar host
Listen on
.Ar host ,
a host name or IP address.
The default is
.Cm localhost ,
which other machines cannot reach.
Use
.Cm 0.0.0.0
to listen on all interfaces.
.It Fl h , -help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl -log-level Ar level
How much to log on standard error:
.Cm error ,
.Cm warn ,
.Cm info
or
.Cm debug .
The default,
.Cm info ,
logs the startup lines, warnings and errors.
.Cm debug
adds a line per request, file system event, reload and live reload
connection.
.It Fl -mermaid-icon-pack Ar pack Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
Let Mermaid diagrams use icons from the named iconify icon packs, such
as
.Cm logos
for
.Ql logos:docker-icon .
The browser fetches a pack from
.Lk https://unpkg.com
the first time a diagram uses one of its icons, so this option needs
network access.
.It Fl -no-border
Render the page without the border around its content.
.It Fl -no-reload
Do not reload pages when files change.
.It Fl p , -port Ar port
Listen on
.Ar port .
Without this option
.Nm
uses port 6419, or the first free port of the twenty that follow when
6419 is busy.
A port given with
.Fl p
is used or fails.
.It Fl v , -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh KEYS
The keys below are shown in the browser by pressing
.Ic \&? .
.Ss Folder page
.Bl -tag -width "Backspace, Esc" -compact
.It Ic Down , j
Next row.
.It Ic Up , k
Previous row.
.It Ic Home , End
First and last row.
.It Ic Enter , Right , l
Open the file or folder.
.It Ic Backspace , Esc , Left , h
Up to the parent folder.
.El
.Ss File page
.Bl -tag -width "Backspace, Esc" -compact
.It Ic Left , h
Previous Markdown file in the folder.
.It Ic Right , l
Next Markdown file in the folder.
.It Ic Esc
Up to the folder.
.El
.Ss Any page
.Bl -tag -width "Backspace, Esc" -compact
.It Ic \&?
Show or hide the list of keys.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Nm
runs until interrupted, for example with Control-C.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Render a README and open it in the browser:
.Pp
.Dl $ preview -b README.md
.Pp
Browse a documentation folder from another machine, on port 8080:
.Pp
.Dl $ preview -H 0.0.0.0 -p 8080 docs/
.Pp
Render without math and Mermaid support:
.Pp
.Dl $ preview -d mathjax,mermaid notes.md
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk https://github.com/troglobit/preview
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
is a fork of go-grip by Christoph Herb, itself a Go reimplementation of
the Python grip by Joe Esposito.
